I've left out both operations requests. Each one needs authority this node isn't granted.

- **Log file append:** The target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI adapter, so the component has no filesystem import. `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` can't be written. Adding a filesystem capability would also change the node's declared world, and its graph signature (`with LLMClient<inference>`) doesn't include one.
- **Metadata fetch:** This would require importing `aap:caps/http-client`, which `ParseMessage` doesn't hold. It would also send the untrusted raw text to an outside service, before this node has discharged its trust. That is exactly the leak the attenuation is meant to prevent.

If operations needs either one, it should be added to the graph as a capability or as a separate node, so the validator can see it.

The node below holds only `inference-llm`. It treats the model's reply as untrusted. An intent label it doesn't recognise becomes `unknown`. The question is cleaned and capped at 512 characters, and entities are bounded.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{raw-message, customer-query};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(message: raw-message) -> customer-query;
}
```

